module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.ClosedPointDirectSumCohomology
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.ClosedPointSupport.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.StrictlyHenselianVanishing

/-!
# Global sections of abelian étale sheaves over a strictly henselian local ring

Let `R` be a strictly henselian local ring and let `s` be a geometric point of `Spec R` lying
over the closed point. The pointed étale neighbourhoods of `s` then have an *initial* object,
namely `Spec R` itself carrying the tautological lift of `s`, so the stalk at `s` — a colimit
over the opposite of that category — is simply the value of the presheaf on the final object of
the small étale site. This file records that comparison and draws the two consequences for
abelian sheaves on the spectrum of a separably closed field `K` that the study of sheaves
supported at closed points needs. There every geometric point lies over the closed point, the
underlying space of `Spec K` having a single point, so every geometric stalk is the module of
global sections: a sheaf with vanishing global sections has all stalks zero, hence vanishes, and
the counit of the constant-sheaf/global-sections adjunction is an epimorphism.

## Main results

* `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.etaleStalkIsoFinalSections` — the geometric stalk at a point over
  the closed point is the value of the presheaf on the final object of the small étale site.
* `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.isZero_etaleStalk_iff_isZero_sections` — the abelian form of that
  comparison: the stalk vanishes exactly when global sections do.
* `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.isZero_of_isZero_sections_final` — on the spectrum of a separably
  closed field an abelian sheaf with vanishing global sections is zero.
* `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.epi_constantSheafΓAdj_counit` — on the spectrum of a separably
  closed field every abelian sheaf is generated by its global sections.

## Implementation notes

The comparison isomorphism is stated for an arbitrary presheaf with values in any category
admitting the colimit defining the stalk: nothing beyond initiality of the final neighbourhood
of `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.nonempty_isInitial_finalNeighborhood` enters, and in particular no
sheaf condition. It is obtained from
`CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit.isIso_ι_app_of_isTerminal` at the opposite of that initial
object, exactly as `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.isIso_globalSectionsToEtaleStalk` does for sheaves
of sets; the value of the restricted diagram at that object is the value of the presheaf on
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.final` on the nose, the first component of
`Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.finalNeighborhood` being that object.

Generation by global sections is proved without computing a single stalk of a constant sheaf.
The counit is an epimorphism as soon as its cokernel vanishes, and the cokernel is detected by
global sections through the previous result; global sections are exact by
`Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.globalSections_preservesFiniteColimits`, so they turn that cokernel
into the cokernel of the image of the counit, which is split epi by the triangle identity of the
adjunction.

Coefficients are `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}` for a site cut out of a big étale site
`B : AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleSite.{u}`, the convention of the surrounding étale-cohomology
files: it is the first coefficient universe in which the site is essentially small, hence the
first in which sheafification, and so the abelian structure used for the cokernel, is
available.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03QO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03QO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.StrictlyHenselian

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (hS : B.Contains (Spec (.of R)))
  (s : GeometricPoint (Spec (.of R)))

/-- **The geometric stalk at a point over the closed point is the value on the final object.**
For `R` strictly henselian local and `s` a geometric point of `Spec R` over the closed point,
the pointed étale neighbourhoods of `s` have an initial object with underlying object
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.final`, so the colimit defining the stalk is attained at that
neighbourhood.

No sheaf condition is used: this is a statement about the shape of the index category, and it
holds for a presheaf with values in any category having the colimit in question. -/
public def etaleStalkIsoFinalSections [StrictlyHenselianLocalRing R]
    (hs : s.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)) {A : Type v} [Category.{w} A]
    (P : (SmallEtale B (Spec (.of R)) hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ A)
    [HasColimit ((Functor.Elements.π (geometricPointFiber B (Spec (.of R)) hS s)).op ⋙ P)] :
    etaleStalk B (Spec (.of R)) hS s P ≅
      P.obj (op (SmallEtale.final B (Spec (.of R)) hS)) :=
  have hι : IsIso (colimit.ι
      ((Functor.Elements.π (geometricPointFiber B (Spec (.of R)) hS s)).op ⋙ P)
      (op (finalNeighborhood B R hS s))) :=
    (colimit.isColimit _).isIso_ι_app_of_isTerminal _
      (IsInitial.op _ (nonempty_isInitial_finalNeighborhood B R hS s hs).some)
  (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ hι).symm

/-- **The geometric stalk at a point over the closed point of a strictly henselian local ring
vanishes exactly when global sections do**, for abelian coefficients. This is the vanishing
form of `Stacks.StrictlyHenselian.etaleStalkIsoFinalSections`. -/
public theorem isZero_etaleStalk_iff_isZero_sections [StrictlyHenselianLocalRing R]
    (hs : s.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R))
    (F : Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of R)) hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    IsZero (etaleStalk B (Spec (.of R)) hS s F.obj) ↔
      IsZero (F.obj.obj (op (SmallEtale.final B (Spec (.of R)) hS))) :=
  ⟨fun h => h.of_iso (etaleStalkIsoFinalSections B R hS s hs F.obj).symm,
    fun h => h.of_iso (etaleStalkIsoFinalSections B R hS s hs F.obj)⟩

/-- **On the spectrum of a separably closed field an abelian étale sheaf with vanishing global
sections is zero.** A separably closed field is a strictly henselian local ring and the
underlying space of its spectrum has a single point, so every geometric point lies over the
closed point and every geometric stalk is the module of global sections; a sheaf with vanishing
geometric stalks is zero. -/
public theorem isZero_of_isZero_sections_final (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (K : Type u) [Field K]
    [IsSepClosed K] (hS : B.Contains (Spec (.of K)))
    (F : Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (h : IsZero (F.obj.obj (op (SmallEtale.final B (Spec (.of K)) hS)))) :
    IsZero F := by
  let : StrictlyHenselianLocalRing K := StrictlyHenselianLocalRing.of_isSepClosed K
  refine isZero_of_forall_isZero_etaleStalk B (Spec (.of K)) hS F fun t => ?_
  exact (isZero_etaleStalk_iff_isZero_sections B K hS t (Subsingleton.elim _ _) F).mpr h

/-- **On the spectrum of a separably closed field every abelian étale sheaf is generated by its
global sections**: the counit of the adjunction between the constant-sheaf functor and global
sections is an epimorphism.

Global sections of the counit are split epi by the triangle identity of the adjunction, and
global sections are exact over a strictly henselian local ring, so they carry the cokernel of
the counit to a vanishing object; a sheaf with vanishing global sections vanishes, so the
cokernel of the counit is zero. -/
public theorem epi_constantSheafΓAdj_counit (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (K : Type u) [Field K]
    [IsSepClosed K] (hS : B.Contains (Spec (.of K)))
    (F : Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    Epi ((constantSheafΓAdj (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).counit.app F) := by
  let : StrictlyHenselianLocalRing K := StrictlyHenselianLocalRing.of_isSepClosed K
  let : IsSplitEpi ((Sheaf.Γ (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).map
      ((constantSheafΓAdj (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS)
        AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).counit.app F)) :=
    IsSplitEpi.mk' ⟨(constantSheafΓAdj (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).unit.app _,
      (constantSheafΓAdj (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS)
        AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).right_triangle_components F⟩
  refine Preadditive.epi_of_isZero_cokernel _ (isZero_of_isZero_sections_final B K hS _ ?_)
  refine IsZero.of_iso ?_ ((Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections
    (SmallEtale.topology B (Spec (.of K)) hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
    (SmallEtale.finalIsTerminal B (Spec (.of K)) hS)).app _).symm
  refine IsZero.of_iso ?_ (PreservesCokernel.iso _ _)
  exact (Preadditive.epi_iff_isZero_cokernel _).mp inferInstance

end Stacks.StrictlyHenselian

end
